| NSWall - Network Appliance Framework for OpenBSD                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+

Thank you for installing NSWall!

QUICK START
-----------

1. Set nswall as the login shell for your admin user:
   # chsh -s /usr/local/bin/nswall admin

2. Or run nswall directly:
   $ nswall

3. Enter privileged mode:
   nswall> enable
   Password: [default: nswall]

4. Configure your system:
   nswall# configure terminal
   nswall(config)# hostname myrouter
   nswall(config)# interface em0
   nswall(config-if)# ip 10.0.0.1/24
   nswall(config-if)# exit
   nswall(config)# write-config

CONFIGURATION FILES
-------------------

  /etc/nswall/nswall.conf     - Main configuration file
  /var/run/nswall/            - Runtime state
  /usr/local/share/nswall/    - Support files

DOCUMENTATION
-------------

  nswall> help                - Show available commands
  nswall> show ?              - Show command options
  nswall# configure ?         - Configuration options

For more information, visit:
  https://github.com/northshorenetworks/NSWall

